    "knowledge_point_id": "3bd2b79a-bc49-5c01-9237-4642e237863f",
    "knowledge_point": "Finding the Image of an Object Under a Combination of Linear Transformations",
    "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062905/assets/4229e1e8c92803a4d51043442a8bc65a6560e11a1e7559af7ec4246fe3005e75.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation that acts on vectors in ${R}^{2}$ as follows (in the order given):\n\n- it shears vectors by a shear factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$ in the $y$-direction, and then\n\n- reflects the result in the $x$-axis.\n\nWhat is the image of the unit square shown above under the action of the linear transformation?",
    "worked_solution": "First, we apply the shear by a shear factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$ in the $y$-direction:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062905/assets/d6d3778b4ef2e343c0aae56478a040eec0d0fb51fda7e997fade27a74ffcb146.png)\n\nThen, we apply the reflection in the $x$-axis:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062905/assets/6d42feee54531cf1381876a908128628cbd2a65ce3701d501bc61ebf63e25c27.png)",
